From 505f12e3d31121f3fa462efa276c588287f7c6b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:35:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(abilities): honor native ability layer priority

Resolve each ability from the highest numbered declaring layer. Explicit
false and zero values own the result; a lower layer must not override them.
Share the ownership lookup between boolean and float consumers so standard
Java ability flags, speed values and native model inputs agree.

Normalize out-of-range serialized layer IDs to Base and retain the latest
entry for a repeated layer. Native packet application clears absent fields
when a later entry replaces that layer, rather than retaining its first row.

Write local flight prediction to Base, matching native flight setters, so a
quick stop before server acknowledgment still sees the pending start. Keep
game-mode fallback values in CustomCache and preserve higher-layer ownership.
Use an explicit layer accessor for both producers.

Evidence: Bedrock 1.26.51.1/build51061372/protocol2193. Original predicate
1434358a0 reads ability index 11 (Instabuild) through actor component lookup
1401d1930. The walk-speed selection at 144762726..1447627a1 uses index 14.
Both scan six layer slots from 5 down to 0. The native ability-name table at
1517ea2b0 identifies their indices. Serialized application 140c4d650 maps
layer IDs directly to those slots, normalizes IDs above 5 to 1, and applies
every entry through 1401d1010 and its original 140cd0cc0 reader. Flight
setters 14d38ada0/14d38ae20 write the Base Flying field at +174/+178; this
setter evidence is static decompilation, not a full actor execution.

Compare 729 complete Instabuild getter cases, 1,305 original walk-speed slices
and 112 complete serialized applications, including actual sparse actor
lookup and per-entry field replacement. The application control observes
an explicit void actor-change notification boundary; actor/Level lifetime,
real game mode delivery and physical flight remain separate verification.
The inventory predicate is Instabuild, independently of creative mode;
full player recipe evaluator and authored-screen integration remain open.
